        "date": "2026-09-13T15:01:11Z"
      },
      "message": "Parse currency-formatted amounts ($1,234.56) when summing\n\nFinance's exports use a dollar sign and thousands separators, which\nfloat() rejects outright. Strip $ and , from the cell before parsing\nit as a number; the raw cell text is still used for grouping and for\nthe non-numeric-cell error message.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
