    "sha": "159c8292ab9e0dadd2b0bfd90473b83b0e8bc832",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOUYQzwtoAKDE1OWM4MjkyYWI5ZTBkYWRkMmIwYmZkOTA0NzNiODNiMGU4YmM4MzI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "factory",
        "email": "factory@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-09-13T15:08:01Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "factory",
        "email": "factory@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-09-13T15:08:01Z"
      },
      "message": "Reject thousands commas that aren't well-formed before stripping\n\nUnconditionally stripping every comma before float() let malformed\nplacements (a European 1.234,56 decimal comma, or a stray 1,3 / 12,34,5)\nsum to a silently wrong result at exit 0 instead of failing loudly. Only\nstrip commas that form a valid thousands grouping (1-3 leading digits,\nthen groups of exactly 3, no comma in the fractional part); anything else\nstill raises TallyError naming the row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
